---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';

const title = 'Portugal Article 90 Residence Permit - Legal Basis for HQA';
const metaTitle = `${title} | Portugal HQA Residency`;
const metaDescription =
  'Portugal Article 90 residence permit is the legal heading for HQA stay. See how Article 90 maps to 2026 requirements and the consular application path.';
---

<Layout title={metaTitle} description={metaDescription}>
  <article>
    <header class="bg-background">
      <div class="site-container py-24 md:py-32">
        <Breadcrumb
          items={[
            { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
            { href: '/portugal-hqa-visa', label: 'Portugal HQA Visa' },
            { label: 'Article 90 residence permit' },
          ]}
        />
        <h1 class="mt-8 max-w-4xl">{title}</h1>
        <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
          Portugal Article 90 residence permit is the legal heading lawyers and hosts often cite for highly qualified activity residence under Portuguese immigration law (Law 23/2007, as amended). The article number is a map reference. It is not a substitute for the current implementing rules, salary floors, or the AIMA and consular document list in force when you file.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>What Article 90 covers in practice</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            Article 90 sits in the statute that governs entry, stay, and removal of foreign nationals. In professional usage it is the hook for a residence permit tied to highly qualified professional activity in Portugal, typically with a Portuguese employer, university, or research host. The operative tests are not the two words “Article 90” on a cover letter. They are the role, the qualifications, the host, and the published conditions that sit under that heading at the date of the decision.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            English marketing copy says HQA. Portuguese filings and legal opinions more often cite the article. Both labels can describe the same permit family. The dictionary of English names is on the
            <a href="/portugal-highly-qualified-activity-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal Highly Qualified Activity visa</a>
            page. The program narrative is on the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal HQA visa</a>
            guide.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-24">
          <h2>How Article 90 relates to an HQA file</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            A complete file still has to show that the activity is highly qualified under the rules that implement the article, and that the applicant can be admitted. That evidence is described, for working purposes, on
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-requirements" class="inline-link">HQA visa requirements</a>.
            How the pack is lodged (consulate or in-country path, biometrics, card issuance) is described on the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-application" class="inline-link">HQA visa application</a>
            page. Article 90 does not pick the consulate for you and does not freeze 2026 processing times.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            Amendments, regulations, and AIMA instructions change what a caseworker actually checks. Treat a citation in an old opinion or a blog post as a starting point. Confirm the current text and the current checklist before you rely on a paragraph number.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-24">
          <h2>What Article 90 does not decide</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            The article number does not turn a real-estate purchase into highly qualified activity. It does not replace a D7 passive-income analysis. It does not, by itself, grant family cards, permanent residence, or citizenship. Those outcomes follow separate statutory tests after a period of legal stay. Citing Article 90 in an email is useful for alignment with counsel. It is not a decision.
          </p>
        </section>

        <div class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
          <a
            href="/portugal-hqa-visa-requirements"
            class="card cluster-card flex h-full flex-col p-8 transition-[transform,box-shadow,border-color] duration-300 ease-out hover:-translate-y-[5px] hover:border-brand hover:shadow-[0_12px_32px_rgba(28,25,23,0.10)]"
          >
            <h3>Requirements that sit under the article</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 flex-1">
              Role, qualifications, host, and the other admission tests used with highly qualified activity residence.
            </p>
            <span class="btn-primary mt-8 w-full gap-2">
              Read the requirements
              <span class="cluster-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </span>
          </a>
          <a
            href="/portugal-hqa-visa-application"
            class="card cluster-card flex h-full flex-col p-8 transition-[transform,box-shadow,border-color] duration-300 ease-out hover:-translate-y-[5px] hover:border-brand hover:shadow-[0_12px_32px_rgba(28,25,23,0.10)]"
          >
            <h3>How the permit is actually filed</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 flex-1">
              Consular and in-country paths, biometrics, and residence-card issuance once the legal heading is the right one.
            </p>
            <span class="btn-primary mt-8 w-full gap-2">
              View the application path
              <span class="cluster-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="bg-cta-tint">
      <div class="site-container flex flex-col items-start gap-6 py-24 md:py-32">
        <h2 class="max-w-3xl">Map Article 90 to the contract and the current checklist</h2>
        <p class="max-w-2xl">
          This page is informational. It is not legal, tax, or immigration advice. Statute citations change. A licensed professional should read the version in force against your host documents.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-cta">Review the Article 90 heading on your file</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
